DTSTART;TZID=/ics.py/2020.1/America/Toronto:20261022T060500
DURATION:PT30M
SUMMARY:Grant submission confirmation: password reset requested\, pending 
 owner input
UID:e004ffcf-e82f-4e0a-9380-e767a31b9f23@e004.org
DESCRIPTION:Verifying the grant submission inside the filing 
 portal\nremained blocked: the account password on record was\nrejected 
 twice and exists nowhere retrievable. With the\nowner's explicit 
 approval\, a password reset was requested\nand the reset email was 
 received and read. Completion\nwaits on the owner entering a password 
 through the secure\nvault card\; after that the agent finishes the 
 reset\,\nsigns in and reads the submission confirmation in one\npass. The 
 in-account confirmation is still unverified\,\nand no password value is 
 recorded anywhere.
DTSTAMP:20261022T215308Z
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART;TZID=/ics.py/2020.1/America/Toronto:20261022T060000
DURATION:PT1H
SUMMARY:onlyspx premarket: pivots run and image trial passed\, posted 
 everywhere
UID:c29219ca-8009-4c2b-be2a-a41bbf768e4e@c292.org
DESCRIPTION:The 6am pivots run succeeded on its first attempt on the\nnew 
 codespace. The image trial's premarket leg passed: the\ncard was generated
  by pasting the day's block into the\nestablished thread\, downloaded at 
 full resolution\, and\nverified number-for-number on the first try\, then 
 shown\nto the owner before posting. The premarket post was\nconfirmed live
  on all five channels.
DTSTAMP:20261022T215308Z
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART;TZID=/ics.py/2020.1/America/Toronto:20261022T065600
DURATION:PT30M
SUMMARY:Google Ads deep dive: account verified\, no-ads card named
UID:03c01949-bada-40a5-8529-5ca9bdc78895@03c0.org
DESCRIPTION:The scheduled morning investigation was blocked at a\nsign-in 
 verification for all accounts\; its Ads deep dive\nwas then completed from
  the main chat at the owner's\ndirection\, with no verification screen 
 appearing. The\ncorrect account identity was verified (an older note 
 had\nconfused two identifiers)\, and the ten ad groups named by\nthe no-
 ads notification were identified: all legacy\nrotation topics in one 
 campaign. Week performance\, assets\,\nrecommendations and change history 
 were reviewed\, and a\nsibling sweep of Search Console\, Analytics and the
  AI\nassistant found nothing new. Read-only\; nothing changed.
DTSTAMP:20261022T215308Z
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART;TZID=/ics.py/2020.1/America/Toronto:20261022T071000
DURATION:PT45M
SUMMARY:Cloud billing account reconciled\; suspension-hold appeal sent
UID:8a591e39-310e-4c38-97b9-53bca65471fc@8a59.org
DESCRIPTION:A cloud billing account was reconciled from mailbox\nrecords 
 against the owner's console figures: the statement\nhistory\, the payments
  already landed\, and the console\ntotal now agree exactly\, with four 
 past-due monthly\ninvoices remaining and a suspension deadline late in 
 the\nmonth. An earlier note claiming the account was cleared\nwas 
 corrected: that payment had cleared only one small\ninvoice. The 
 receivables correspondence was read in full\,\nand an appeal email making 
 the nonprofit case with an\nagreed catch-up plan was drafted\, shown to 
 the owner\,\nrevised twice at his direction\, and sent. Reply awaited.
DTSTAMP:20261022T215308Z
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART;TZID=/ics.py/2020.1/America/Toronto:20261022T082000
DURATION:PT1H
SUMMARY:Stern professors: pages re-checked live\, download pattern mapped
UID:e73f444f-f74a-4f0a-a51e-f5791139d8cb@e73f.org
DESCRIPTION:After the owner pushed back on an earlier sweep verdict\,\nthe 
 richest professor pages at one business school were\nre-verified live with
  file-link counts\, and a side-by-side\ncheck compared the leading page 
 against two peers. Files\nlive inside each professor's own site space 
 (papers\, CV\nand course subfolders)\; there is no central 
 repository.\nContent is almost all research papers\; slides appear 
 once\nand datasets are effectively one professor only. The\nverdict 
 stands: one professor runs the only\nsession-by-session course library. 
 Teaching lines were\ncompiled from the professors' own pages.
DTSTAMP:20261022T215308Z
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART;TZID=/ics.py/2020.1/America/Toronto:20261022T090000
DURATION:PT30M
SUMMARY:Oct 15 application follow-ups: no replies\, six drafts written
UID:e4292939-0931-4d26-b40a-829507a284fb@e429.org
DESCRIPTION:The seven-day follow-up run for the six applications\nsubmitted
  on October 15 checked the mailbox in full: no\nreply\, rejection or 
 invitation from any of the six\nemployers since submission\; only 
 submission-day\nconfirmations\, one of them verified in detail. 
 Six\napproval-ready follow-up drafts were written using\nportal-first 
 channels only. Nothing was sent. The next\ncheckpoint is October 29.
DTSTAMP:20261022T215308Z
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART;TZID=/ics.py/2020.1/America/Toronto:20261022T094500
DURATION:PT3H
SUMMARY:onlyspx gap: posted everywhere\, image rejected\, then repaired
UID:bcb1666e-580d-4cf5-be9d-beba042813e6@bcb1.org
DESCRIPTION:The 9:45 gap run succeeded on its first attempt. The 
 image\ntrial's gap leg failed verification twice: downloads from\nthe 
 established thread repeatedly served old cards\, and a\nscreenshot 
 recovery was substituted and verified for\nnumbers only. Posting completed
  on all five channels\, but\nthe owner then rejected the gap image quality
  (low\nresolution\, a cursor artifact baked in). Repair: the\nowner's own 
 verified full card was posted to the image\nchannels\, the old video-
 platform post was deleted and\nreplaced\, and the old photo post still 
 awaits deletion in\nhis app (the API cannot delete). A new standing 
 rule\nrequires a continuity-and-likeness check against previous\nposts in 
 a series before anything goes out\, and the gap\nrun was hardened with a 
 no-screenshot rule.
DTSTAMP:20261022T215308Z
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART;TZID=/ics.py/2020.1/America/Toronto:20261022T095000
DURATION:PT40M
SUMMARY:Hosting breach disclosed\; owner handling credential rotation
UID:8008716e-5621-4a33-9cdc-da86197d441a@8008.org
DESCRIPTION:A hosting platform disclosed overnight that stored\nenvironment
  variables may have been exposed\, and it\ninvalidated all API tokens. The
  exposed services were\ninventoried\, including the Monday rotation 
 service\, an\noffline colleague agent with stored credentials\, and 
 a\nparked fleet of services. The owner chose to handle the\ncredential 
 rotation himself\; a priority checklist was\nhanded to him and the agent 
 does not touch the\ncredentials. Separately\, an AI provider 
 proactively\ndisabled one exposed key\, and an unfamiliar sign-in to\nthat
  account was confirmed by the owner as his contractor\nteam\, not an 
 intrusion.
DTSTAMP:20261022T215308Z
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART;TZID=/ics.py/2020.1/America/Toronto:20261022T121000
DURATION:PT1H
SUMMARY:Video library: hand-picked queue drained
UID:8186469c-97e2-4d88-a71c-524102b62e94@8186.org
DESCRIPTION:The hand-picked additions queue was fully drained: two\nentries
  completed with full transcripts and resources\,\nincluding one entry's 
 complete set of 48 spreadsheets\nharvested and classified under the source
  page's sections.\nLibrary totals updated and all commits pushed. A 
 lesson\nwas recorded: never stage downloads in temporary storage\n(a 
 cleanup destroyed a verified batch mid-work and it had\nto be re-
 downloaded)\; stage under the workspace.
DTSTAMP:20261022T215308Z
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART;TZID=/ics.py/2020.1/America/Toronto:20261022T141300
DURATION:PT2H
SUMMARY:Google Ads Target Rotation: execution pass completed
UID:ac95d589-0103-40b1-a3db-fefdc9fafa89@ac95.org
DESCRIPTION:The owner set the division of labor (Target Rotation is\nthis 
 desk\; the brand campaigns belong to a colleague) and\nruled that 
 superseded rotation groups are paused\, never\ndeleted\, so their keywords
  and history survive. A\nsearch-terms audit of nearly a thousand terms 
 found the\njunk traffic arrives mainly through AI expansion beyond\nthe 
 keyword lists. Execution\, all verified live: the\nbroad-match auto-apply 
 was turned off\; the nine legacy\ngroups were paused\; negatives were 
 added for a symptom\ncluster\, an election-poll cluster\, a piracy-list 
 phrase\nand one exact term\; AI Max was turned off for the 
 Target\ncampaign only. The platform refused two negatives because\nthose 
 terms are targeted keywords inside their own group\;\nremoving them is the
  owner's pending decision. Keyword\nlists for the seven Paper groups found
  holding zero\nkeywords were presented for approval\; nothing loaded yet.
DTSTAMP:20261022T215308Z
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART;TZID=/ics.py/2020.1/America/Toronto:20261022T170000
DURATION:PT30M
SUMMARY:Icarus appraisal replies watch: no new replies
UID:0c20238b-9d4f-4e93-87f4-75640625867e@0c20.org
DESCRIPTION:The replies watch checked the mailbox for valuation\nresponses:
  only the two already-reported October replies\nplus the owner's own 
 outbound messages were found. No new\nsubstantive reply and no estimate 
 yet\; two parties remain\nsilent. The watch continues.
DTSTAMP:20261022T215308Z
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART;TZID=/ics.py/2020.1/America/Toronto:20261029T090000
DURATION:PT30M
SUMMARY:Job applications: Oct 15 batch +14-day checkpoint
UID:ea89e373-9af9-4615-a208-342703a02e6e@ea89.org
DESCRIPTION:Check for employer replies to the six applications submitted on
  October 15\; follow-up drafts are staged and nothing is sent without the 
 owner's word.
DTSTAMP:20261022T215308Z
END:VEVENT
